From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:13:40 +0800
Subject: core/compaction: checkpoint strategy, written as a follow-up to the
 live context

`compaction.strategy: "checkpoint"` (default "summary", upstream's) changes local compaction:

- When: at 90% of the window, but never above 540k tokens (`compaction.threshold.ratio` /
  `.tokens`), and never above the summary strategy's ceiling, which keeps room for the reply.
- How: the live context goes out exactly as the last step sent it, with the checkpoint prompt
  appended as a user message, so the whole prefix is a cache read. Tools and tool_choice stay as
  they are, since changing them would invalidate the cached messages. Upstream sends only the
  older part, which ends where no request put a cache breakpoint.
- What: pi's checkpoint sections (goal, constraints, progress, key decisions, next steps,
  critical context) with OpenCode's rules (no AGENTS.md or environment, at most 15 relevant
  files, open requests in the user's words, git state), plus "Running" for work still going
  outside the conversation. Every compaction writes a fresh checkpoint: an earlier one is
  history to carry forward only while still true, never a draft to update.
- Guards: a reply that calls a tool, lacks the template (6 of the 9 sections), or is too short
  gets one reminder; a second failure falls back to the summary strategy. A response silent for
  `compaction.timeout` ms (default 300000, pi's HTTP idle timeout; 0 disables) is retried under
  the session's retry policy. Overflow recovery always takes the summary path, since the live
  context no longer fits.

The recent part is still kept as upstream keeps it (text beside the summary); the prompt names
where it starts.

Ocelot-Patch: core/checkpoint-compaction

